From: Monea Software <build@hdsatelit.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] GStreamer: hdsdvb board sinks preroll (e2-async) for playbin3 and MSE

The OE-Alliance dvbvideosink and dvbaudiosink start with sync and async off
and ignore the "sync" and "async" properties; only e2-sync and e2-async,
set by the receiver player, change them. With playbin3, which Media Source
Extensions always use, playsink waits for the sink to preroll: without it
the video chain stays in READY and the first buffer fails with
"gst_pad_push() returned error". The legacy playbin did not need it.

The receiver decoder loan now sets e2-async to TRUE on the board sinks it
creates (sync stays as it is).

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [satellite receiver configuration]

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/gstreamer/GStreamerHdsDvbDecoder.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/gstreamer/GStreamerHdsDvbDecoder.cpp
@@ -182,6 +182,13 @@
         return nullptr;
     }
 
+    // The board sinks start with sync and async off and ignore the "sync" and "async" properties: only the e2-sync and
+    // e2-async properties of the receiver player change them. playbin3, which Media Source Extensions always use, needs a
+    // sink that prerolls (async), otherwise playsink never reaches PAUSED and the first buffers fail. The legacy playbin
+    // did not need it.
+    if (gstObjectHasProperty(sink, "e2-async"_s))
+        g_object_set(sink, "e2-async", TRUE, nullptr);
+
     m_sinkCount++;
     g_object_weak_ref(G_OBJECT(sink), sinkFinalized, this);
     GST_DEBUG("%s created, %u board sinks", factoryName.characters(), m_sinkCount);
